### Page 1 of 4

```text
1
ORDINANCE NO. ___________
ENTITLED:
“AN ORDINANCE AMENDING, REPEALING, AND CREATING CERTAIN
SECTIONS OF CHAPTER 10.52, STOPPING, STANDING AND PARKING
GENERALLY, OF TITLE 10, VEHICLES AND TRAFFIC, OF THE CODE OF
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, RELATING TO THE PARKING OF
RECREATIONAL VEHICLES AND TRAILERS.”
BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:
Section 1.  That Section 10.52.020, Prohibited in specified places, of Chapter 10.52,
Stopping, Standing and Parking Generally, of Title 10, Vehicles and Traffic, of the Code of the City
of Cheyenne, Wyoming, is hereby created as follows:
Section 10.52.020
Prohibited in specified places.
Except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic, or in compliance with law or the
direction of a police officer or other official traffic-control devices, no person shall:
A.
Stop, stand or park a vehicle:
1.
Which is a tractor unit with ten (10) or more wheels and/or a fifth wheel, with
or without a semitrailer, upon any street or alley in the city, except when such vehicles are
in the process of loading or unloading at the site of origin or delivery of shipments;
recreational campers and vans may park for the time limits posted.
Any person found guilty of violating subsection (A)(1) of this section shall be fined
not less than one hundred dollars ($100.00),
2.
(This paragraph remains unchanged)
3.
(This paragraph remains unchanged)
4.
(This paragraph remains unchanged)

B.
Stand or park a vehicle OR TRAILER, whether occupied or not:
1.
Within six FIFTEEN (15) feet of a fire hydrant,
2.
(This paragraph remains unchanged.)
3.
UNLESS OTHERWISE POSTED, STAND OR PARK A MOTOR
VEHICLE, TRAILER OR OTHER OBJECT, OR ANY PART THEREOF, WITHIN
THIRTY (30) FEET OF ANY POINT FORMED BY THE INTERSECTION OF THE
CURB LINES EXTENDING FROM ANY CORNER OF THE INTERSECTION.  FOR
THE PURPOSES OF THIS SUBSECTION, “CURB LINE” IS DEFINED AS THE LINE
COINCIDENT WITH THE FACE OF THE STREET CURB ADJACENT TO THE
ROADWAY.
3. 4.
(This paragraph remains unchanged.)
4. 5.
In front of or within five (5) feet of a public or private driveway, and AN
alley, OR A RAMP TO PROVIDE ACCESS FOR PERSONS WITH PHYSICAL
DISABILITIES.
5. 6.
(This paragraph remains unchanged.)
```

### Page 2 of 4

```text
2
6. 7.
(This paragraph remains unchanged.)
C.
Park a vehicle, whether occupied or not:
1.
Within twenty (20) FIFTY (50) feet of the nearest rail of a railroad crossing.
Section 2.
That Section 10.52.030, Parking not to obstruct traffic, of Chapter 10.52,
Stopping Standing, and Parking Generally, of Title 10, Vehicles and Traffic, of the Code of the City
of Cheyenne is hereby amended as follows:
Section 10.52.030
Parking not to obstruct traffic.
No person shall park any vehicle upon a street, other than an alley, in such a manner or under
such conditions as to leave available less than ten (10) feet of the width of the roadway, as measured
from the centerline OR CENTERLINE pavement marking, for free movement of vehicular traffic.

Section 3.
That Section 10.52.190, Parking prohibited at all times, Section 10.52.200,
Parking prohibited during certain hours, and Section 10.52.210, Stopping, standing or parking
prohibited during certain hours, of Chapter 10.52, Stopping, Standing and Parking Generally, of Title
10, Vehicles and Traffic, of the Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, are hereby repealed:
Section 10.52.190
Parking prohibited at all times.
Repealed in its entirety, including Schedule D.
Section 10.52.200
Parking prohibited during certain hours.
Repealed in its entirety, including Schedule E.
Section 10.52.210
Stopping, standing or parking prohibited during certain hours.
Repealed in its entirety, including Schedule F.
Section 4.
That Section 10.52.190, Designating and posting of prohibited parking, of
Chapter 10.52, Stopping, Standing and Parking Generally, of Title 10, Vehicles and Traffic, of the
Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, is hereby created as follows:
Section 10.52.190
DESIGNATING AND POSTING OF PROHIBITED PARKING.
IN ADDITION TO THE GENERAL PROHIBITIONS STATED IN THIS CHAPTER, THE
CITY ENGINEER, OR HIS OR HER DESIGNEE, IS HEREBY AUTHORIZED, IN
ACCORDANCE WITH APPLICABLE STATE AND FEDERAL STATUTES, RULES AND
REGULATIONS, TO DESIGNATE AND POST PROHIBITIONS, LIMITATIONS,
REGULATIONS AND EXCEPTIONS THERETO, REGARDING THE PARKING OF
VEHICLES, RECREATIONAL VEHICLES, AND TRAILERS WITHIN THE CITY LIMITS OF
CHEYENNE.
Section 5.  That Section 10.52.200, Recreational vehicle, Trailer–Defined; Parking permitted
in certain places, of Chapter 10.52, Stopping, Standing and Parking Generally, of Title 10, Vehicles
and Traffic, of the Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, is hereby created as follows:
Section 10.52.200
RECREATIONAL VEHICLE, TRAILER–DEFINED; PARKING
PERMITTED IN CERTAIN PLACES.
A.
FOR PURPOSES OF THIS CHAPTER, “RECREATIONAL VEHICLE (RV)”
MEANS ANY OF THE FOLLOWING:
```

### Page 3 of 4

```text
3
1.
A VEHICULAR, PORTABLE STRUCTURE BUILT ON A CHASSIS,
DESIGNED TO BE USED AS A TEMPORARY DWELLING FOR TRAVEL, IN
ACCORDANCE WITH ANSI STANDARDS BULLETIN NO. 119-A;
2.
A PICKUP CAMPER, MEANING A STRUCTURE DESIGNED TO BE
MOUNTED ON A TRUCK CHASSIS, FOR USE AS A TEMPORARY DWELLING FOR
TRAVEL, RECREATION AND VACATION;
3.
A MOTOR HOME, MEANING A PORTABLE, TEMPORARY
DWELLING, TO BE USED FOR TRAVEL, RECREATION OR VACATION,
CONSTRUCTED AS AN INTEGRAL PART OF A SELF-PROPELLED VEHICLE;
4.
A CAMPING TRAILER, MEANING A STRUCTURE MOUNTED ON
WHEELS AND DESIGNED TO BE USED FOR TRAVEL, RECREATION OR
VACATION; OR
5.
A BOAT OR TRAILER OF ANY TYPE, THAT IS OVER TWENTY (20)
FEET LONG, MEASURED FROM THE TONGUE, OR OVER FOUR AND ONE-HALF
(4½) FEET HIGH, INCLUDING ANY LOAD THEREON.
B.
FOR THE PURPOSES OF THIS CHAPTER, “TRAILER” MEANS ANY OF THE
FOLLOWING:
1.
ANY “SEMI-TRAILER” WHICH IS DESIGNED FOR CARRYING
PERSONS OR PROPERTY AND FOR BEING DRAWN BY A MOTOR VEHICLE AND
SO CONSTRUCTED THAT SOME PART OF ITS WEIGHT OR THAT OF ITS LOAD
RESTS UPON OR IS CARRIED BY ANOTHER VEHICLE.  “SEMI-TRAILER” SHALL
INCLUDE ANY CAMPER DESIGNED TO BE CARRIED IN OR UPON A TRUCK OR
OTHER MOTOR VEHICLE, AND ANY HOUSE TRAILER, AS DEFINED BY WYO.
STAT. ANN. § 31-5-102(a)(xv), IF SO DESIGNED OR CONSTRUCTED THAT SOME
PART OF ITS WEIGHT OR THAT OF ITS LOAD RESTS UPON OR IS CARRIED BY
ANOTHER VEHICLE.
2.
ANY “TRAILER” WHICH IS DESIGNED FOR CARRYING PERSONS OR
PROPERTY AND FOR BEING DRAWN BY A MOTOR VEHICLE AND SO
CONSTRUCTED THAT NO PART OF ITS WEIGHT OR THAT OF ITS LOAD RESTS
UPON OR IS CARRIED BY ANOTHER VEHICLE.  “TRAILER” SHALL INCLUDE
ANY CAMP TRAILER, TENT TRAILER, OR HOUSE TRAILER, AS DEFINED BY
WYO.  STAT. ANN. § 31-5-102(a)(xv), IF SO DESIGNED OR CONSTRUCTED THAT
NO PART OF ITS WEIGHT OR THAT OF ITS LOAD RESTS UPON OR IS CARRIED
BY ANOTHER VEHICLE.
C.
SUBJECT TO LIMITATIONS SPECIFIED IN THIS CHAPTER, ONE (1)
RECREATIONAL VEHICLE OR TRAILER MAY BE PARKED ON A STREET IN THE CITY
WITH THE CONSENT OF THE OWNER OR OWNERS OF THE REAL PROPERTY WHICH
IS IMMEDIATELY ADJACENT TO THE RIGHT-OF-WAY IN WHICH THE RECREATIONAL
VEHICLE OR TRAILER IS PARKED.
```

